-- Re-association must not steal expressions that already have a meaning.
-- A registered n-ary mixfix pattern whose flat shape coincides with an
-- operator chain keeps its n-ary interpretation, even when every keyword in
-- it is also a fixity-declared binary operator.

@infixl 6
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
      q IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
p andop q MEANS p + q

@infixl 6
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
      q IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
p hadop q MEANS p * q

-- the ternary pattern `_ andop _ hadop _` predates re-association and wins
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
a andop b hadop c MEANS 1000 + a + b + c

-- ternary interpretation: 1000 + 1 + 2 + 3 = 1006
-- (re-association would have produced 1 + 2 * 3 = 7)
#EVAL 1 andop 2 hadop 3

-- keyword-first n-ary mixfix is likewise untouched
GIVEN c IS A BOOLEAN
      t IS A NUMBER
      e IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
myif c mythen t myelse e MEANS IF c THEN t ELSE e

#EVAL myif TRUE mythen 42 myelse 7

-- A subtler theft: an n-ary pattern with CONSECUTIVE param slots
-- (`_ quop _ _ _`) matches the same flat App shape as a `quop`/`opdue`
-- chain, because the `opdue` operator marker is consumed as an ordinary
-- argument (here a function-typed one). The old guard only checked the
-- alternating canonical name `_ quop _ opdue _` and so did NOT decline; the
-- fixed guard dry-runs the real matcher and declines whenever any registered
-- pattern engages this flat shape.
@infixl 6
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
      q IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
p quop q MEANS p + q

@infixl 7
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
      q IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
p opdue q MEANS p * q

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      f IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER AND NUMBER TO NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
a quop b f d MEANS 100 + a + b + d

-- quaternary interpretation: f = the `opdue` operator, result 100 + 1 + 2 + 3
-- = 106 — NOT re-association to 1 quop (2 opdue 3) = 7, even though both quop
-- and opdue carry @infixl declarations
#EVAL 1 quop 2 opdue 3
